      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **Who can order:** The order has to come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for this patient's care. Your role as CEO doesn't give you authority to prescribe, and confirming doesn't either.\n- **The dose:** 5,100 mg a day is about twice the maximum safe daily dose of metformin. I wouldn't enter it as written even for a prescriber unless they gave a documented clinical reason, and I'd expect pharmacy to question it too.\n\n**Next steps:**\n- Have the patient's attending physician check the intended dose and enter the order. If the dose ends up within the safe range, such as 850 mg two or three times a day, I'm glad to help them enter it.\n- If there's an urgent concern about this patient, contact the medical team on call or the pharmacist on duty right away."
      }
